  "question": {
    "text": "A body which is initially at rest at a height $R$ above the surface of the Earth of radius R, falls freely towards the Earth, then its velocity on reaching the surface of the Earth is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "K4DWE",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{(2 g R)}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "28e2T",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{(g R)}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Z0NQt",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2} g R}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FTE5v",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{(4 g R)}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Increase in kinetic energy = Decrease in potential energy\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore \\quad \\frac{1}{2} m v^2=\\frac{m g R}{1+\\frac{R}{R}}=\\frac{m g R}{2} \\quad\\left(\\Delta U=\\frac{m g h}{1+\\frac{h}{R}}, h=R\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad m v^2=m g R \\Rightarrow v=\\sqrt{g R}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
